cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Fatigue-driven structural reuse assessment of a decommissioned
  OC4 offshore wind jacket
message: >-
  If you use this software, its results or its figures, please cite it
  using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kenneweg
    given-names: Gregor Elias
    affiliation: University College Cork
abstract: >-
  Code, results and documentation from an MEng dissertation assessing how
  much of a decommissioned offshore wind jacket substructure could be
  reused. A 414-run OpenFAST campaign over the OC4 reference jacket
  carrying the NREL 5MW turbine feeds a fatigue post-processing pipeline
  producing per-member and per-joint damage maps, a corrosion trajectory
  to 25 years, a static/ULS check, and an L0-L4 reuse classification.
  Finds that the static check rather than fatigue governs remaining life
  for most members, and that splash-zone joints are the binding
  constraint on reuse.
keywords:
  - offshore wind
  - jacket substructure
  - fatigue
  - structural reuse
  - circular economy
  - decommissioning
  - OpenFAST
  - OC4
  - NREL 5MW
  - embodied carbon
